Fix an infinite recursion in Qlementine 1.4.2's QComboBox event filter.

`ComboboxItemViewFilter::eventFilter` handles `QEvent::ChildAdded` on the
combo box and compares the added child with `_comboBox->view()`. Calling
`view()` creates the private popup container if it does not exist yet, which
emits another `ChildAdded` event and re-enters the same filter. With Qt 6.8.3
the result is an unbounded recursion and a stack overflow (0xC00000FD) as
soon as a QComboBox is constructed.

The filter already stores the view it was created for in `_view`; compare
against that pointer instead of asking the combo box to create/look up its
view again.

--- a/lib/src/style/eventFilters/ComboboxItemViewFilter.hpp
+++ b/lib/src/style/eventFilters/ComboboxItemViewFilter.hpp
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ protected:
         if (watchedObject == _comboBox) {
           const auto* childEvent = static_cast<QChildEvent*>(evt);
           const auto* child = childEvent->child();
-          if (child == _comboBox->view()) {
+          if (child == _view) {
             if (auto* qlementine = qobject_cast<QlementineStyle*>(_comboBox->style())) {
               _comboBox->setItemDelegate(new ComboBoxDelegate(_comboBox, *qlementine));
             }
